{
  "adjBlack": "These squares (6, 3, 1 and 2) touch a purple square (outlined), and purple squares can't touch, so they must be clear.",
  "boxedIn": "This 6 is the outlined clear square's last neighbor that isn't purple, so it must be clear to keep that square joined.",
  "corner2": "A touching pair of 4s sits at the corner, so one must be purple. Shading this 2 would force the 4 beside the corner purple, leaving the corner 1 boxed in, so it must stay clear.",
  "corner3": "This inner 3 matches both outlined 3s flanking the outlined corner 6; keeping it clear would make both purple and box the corner in, so it must be purple.",
  "corner4": "This corner 5 matches both its outlined neighbors; keeping it clear would make both purple and box it in, so it and the 5 diagonally inside must be purple.",
  "offset": "There's a pair of 2s in one column and another pair in the next, lined up so that shading the ringed 5 would force two of the 2s to be purple next to each other, and purple squares can't touch, so it must be clear.",
  "oneCell": "The outlined 6s sit one square apart, so one of them must be purple: the 2 between them must be clear.",
  "pair": "The outlined 4s touch, so one of them stays clear and uses up the 4 in this row: the ringed 4 must be purple.",
  "sameLine": "This 2 shares this row with the outlined clear 2, which already uses that number, so it must be purple.",
  "sandwich": "The outlined 6s sit one square apart, so one of them must be purple: the 2 between them must be clear.",
  "sharedLine": "This 2 shares this row with the outlined clear 2, which already uses that number, so it must be purple.",
  "split": "Shading this 4 would cut some of the outlined squares off from the rest of the clear region, so it must be clear.",
  "twoCells": "These 4s share this column with the outlined clear 4, which already uses that number, so they must be purple.",
}
`;
